        "narrative": "<p>Shallow water populations are dominated by walleye and northern pike.  Deep water populations are dominated by small cisco and average sized whitefish.  Populations of all species appear to be stable.  Some very large lake trout and northern pike are present.Fishing pressure is not known but is thought to be light.  This is a clear lake with steep dropoffs along the shore, and is not easy to fish. Its remoteness also probably limits angling pressure.</p>",
